        "date": "2026-11-10T02:16:30Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): a lathe thread's spindle arcs are judged by radius in the travel check\n\n#631: the built-in Lathe (X 0..320) refused every thread - its passes\nare arcs about the spindle axis, whose far side and quarter points read\nnegative X (the CL's antipode; the spindle turns the work, the slide\nnever goes there). On a lathe, an XY arc centred on the spindle axis is\nnow judged in X by its radius; every other move keeps its signed X, so\na real past-centre over-travel is still refused.\n\nPinned by lathe_thread_travel (2): a thread passes the built-in Lathe\n(fails without the fix with the issue's message), and the same thread\non a 0..2 mm X stroke is refused in X.\n\nFixes #631\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
